     {
      "word": "بَرْنَامَج",
      "register": "neutral",
      "nuance": "programme, schedule — a plan of activities"
     },
     {
      "word": "مَشْرُوع",
      "register": "neutral",
      "nuance": "project, a planned undertaking"
     }
    ],
    "antonyms": [],
    "etymology": {
     "text": "Root خ ط ط “to draw a line”; Wiktionary: project, projected course, plan; plural خُطَط. خَطّ “line, handwriting” shares the root.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "خَطّ, a line (also handwriting and a bus line), is the same root: a plan is a line drawn ahead."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "خِطَّة (ḫiṭṭa, with i) is a plot of land, a district — another word with the same letters."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "“To plan” is خَطَّطَ (form II) with لِـ: خَطَّطْنَا لِلرِّحْلَةِ “we planned the trip”."
    ]
